  (text "═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                       TEST & DEBUG INFRASTRUCTURE (Rev 2.0)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

ARCHITECTURE CHANGE (Rev 2.0):
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  DELETED (no MCU on headstage):
    • J_DEBUG (TC2030-IDC) — SWD debug header removed
    • SWDIO, SWCLK, SWO signals — removed
    • RESET_N via debug header — removed (RESET still on B2B)
    • TP_LVDS0 — LVDS test point removed (no LVDS on headstage)

  KEPT (essential for analog debug):
    • Input shorting via ADG1414 switches
    • Calibration injection circuit
    • Power isolation resistors
    • Power rail test points
    • SPI signal test points (updated for DDR MISO)

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
1. INPUT SHORTING (Noise Floor Measurement)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  TEST_SHORT_EN (from carrier FPGA via B2B connector)
         │
         ▼
  ┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
  │      CMOS Switch Array              │
  │      ADG1414 (×16 for 128ch)        │
  │                                     │
  CH1 ───┤IN1                      COM ├───► VREF (1.65V)
  CH2 ───┤IN2                          │
  ...    │                             │
  CH8 ───┤IN8                          │
  │      └─────────────────────────────┘
  │
  └──► When TEST_SHORT_EN = HIGH, all inputs shorted to VREF
       Measure noise floor with known zero-signal condition

COMPONENT:
  ADG1414: 8-channel SPST switch, <1Ω Ron, <1nA leakage
  Need 16× ADG1414 for 128 channels
  Power: VDD = VIN (3.3–5V), logic input from B2B control line
  Control: Single TEST_SHORT_EN line controls all 16 ICs
           (directly connected, no MCU GPIO needed)

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2. CALIBRATION INJECTION (Gain/BW/Mapping Verification)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  CAL_SRC (from carrier FPGA via B2B — square wave or sine)
         │
         ▼
  R_ATTEN (100kΩ) ──┬── R_DIV (100Ω) ──► CAL_OUT
                     │
                    GND

  Attenuation: 1000:1
  If carrier outputs 1Vpp square wave → CAL_OUT = 1mVpp
  Realistic spike-like amplitude for testing

  CAL_OUT routed to injection point via:
  • Dedicated AUX_IN on RHD2164 (preferred path)
  • Or capacitively coupled to selected channels

  CAL_EN (from carrier via B2B) enables injection circuit
  via series analog switch (ADG1419 or similar SPST)

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
3. POWER ISOLATION (Analog/Digital Debug Separation)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  VIN ──[R_ISO1 0Ω]──► To ADP151 LDO ──► AVDD

  Remove R_ISO1 to disconnect analog supply for isolated testing.
  (DVDD_AFE is derived from VIN via ferrite, not a separate LDO,
   so it is also disabled when R_ISO1 is removed.)

  NOTE: Rev 1.0 had R_ISO2 for separate DVDD isolation.
        With the simplified power tree (no MCU LDO), a single
        isolation point at VIN is sufficient.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════"
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 20 20)
    (effects
      (font (size 1.2 1.2))
      (justify left)
    )
  )

  (text "TEST POINT TABLE (Rev 2.0)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Ref         Net           Location          Purpose
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
TP_VIN      VIN           Near B2B conn     Input voltage from carrier
TP_AVDD     AVDD          Near LDO output   Analog rail, noise measurement
TP_DVDD_AFE DVDD_AFE      After ferrite     Filtered digital rail for AFE
TP_VREF     VREF          Near RHD2164      Reference voltage (1.225V)
TP_GND      GND           Near B2B conn     Ground reference for probes
TP_SCLK     SCLK          At fan-out node   SPI clock from carrier
TP_MISO1A   MISO1_A       Near U1           DDR MISO A from RHD2164 #1
TP_MISO1B   MISO1_B       Near U1           DDR MISO B from RHD2164 #1
TP_MISO2A   MISO2_A       Near U2           DDR MISO A from RHD2164 #2
TP_CAL      CAL_OUT       After attenuator  Cal injection verification
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

DELETED from Rev 1.0:
  TP_DVDD   — replaced by TP_DVDD_AFE (no MCU DVDD rail)
  TP_MISO1  — split into TP_MISO1A + TP_MISO1B (DDR dual MISO)
  TP_MISO2  — split into TP_MISO2A + TP_MISO2B (only A shown, B optional)
  TP_LVDS0  — removed (no LVDS on headstage)

Test points: 1mm pads, plated, no soldermask
             Accessible from top layer, not under components
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"
